  "08-tools_lab-1-crewai-agents": {
    "title": "Lab 8.1: CrewAI \u2014 Multi-Agent Teams in Config",
    "module": "Module 8: Tools",
    "duration": "20 min",
    "instructions": "# Lab 8.1: CrewAI \u2014 Multi-Agent Teams in Config\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n                     config.yaml\n                         \u2502\n              \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n              \u25bc          \u25bc          \u25bc\n         \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510 \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n         \u2502Research\u2502\u2192\u2502 Writer \u2502\u2192\u2502Reviewer\u2502\n         \u2502 Agent  \u2502 \u2502 Agent  \u2502 \u2502 Agent  \u2502\n         \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518 \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518 \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n              \u2502                      \u2502\n              \u25bc                      \u25bc\n         \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510           \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n         \u2502 Tools  \u2502           \u2502 Output \u2502\n         \u2502(search)\u2502           \u2502(report)\u2502\n         \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518           \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n\n## Why\n\nYou don't build agent orchestration from scratch.\nCrewAI = define agents + tasks in config, Python is just glue.\nSwap agents, reorder tasks, add tools \u2014 all without touching code.\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\npip install crewai crewai-tools\nmake run topic=\"Kubernetes autoscaling for AI agents\"\n```\n\n## What You'll Do\n\n1. Read `config.yaml` \u2014 agents, tasks, process order\n2. `make run` \u2014 watch 3 agents collaborate\n3. Edit config: change an agent's model, add a task, swap order\n4. Challenge: Add a 4th agent (FactChecker) between writer and reviewer\n5. Challenge: Switch process to \"hierarchical\" (one agent manages others)\n\n## Key Insight\n\nThe Python file (`crew.py`) is 25 lines. All intelligence is in config.\n",
    "config_file": "config.yaml",
    "config_content": "# \u2500\u2500\u2500 CrewAI Agent Config \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n# Define agents + tasks in YAML. Python just loads and runs this.\n\nagents:\n  researcher:\n    role: \"Research Analyst\"\n    goal: \"Find accurate, relevant information\"\n    backstory: \"Expert at searching knowledge bases and summarizing findings\"\n    llm: gpt-4o-mini\n    tools:\n      - web_search\n      - qdrant_search\n    verbose: true\n\n  writer:\n    role: \"Technical Writer\"\n    goal: \"Produce clear, actionable reports\"\n    backstory: \"Skilled at turning complex research into simple explanations\"\n    llm: gpt-4o-mini\n    tools: []\n    verbose: true\n\n  reviewer:\n    role: \"Quality Reviewer\"\n    goal: \"Catch errors, verify claims, improve clarity\"\n    backstory: \"Meticulous editor who ensures accuracy and completeness\"\n    llm: gpt-4o\n    tools:\n      - web_search\n    verbose: true\n\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500 Tasks (what to do, in order) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\ntasks:\n  research:\n    description: \"Research {topic}: find key facts, recent developments, and best practices\"\n    agent: researcher\n    expected_output: \"Bullet list of 5-10 key findings with sources\"\n\n  write_report:\n    description: \"Write a 500-word report based on research findings\"\n    agent: writer\n    expected_output: \"Structured report with intro, findings, recommendations\"\n    context: [research]    # This task gets output from 'research'\n\n  review:\n    description: \"Review the report for accuracy, clarity, and completeness\"\n    agent: reviewer\n    expected_output: \"Final report with corrections applied\"\n    context: [write_report]\n\n# \u2500\u2500\u2500 Crew Settings \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\ncrew:\n  process: sequential          # sequential | hierarchical\n  max_rpm: 10                  # Rate limit to avoid API throttling\n  memory: true                 # Agents remember within session\n  verbose: true\n",
    "run_file": "crew.py",
    "run_content": "\"\"\"\ncrew.py \u2014 25 lines. Config does the thinking.\n\"\"\"\nimport yaml\nfrom crewai import Agent, Task, Crew, Process\n\n# Load config\nwith open(\"config.yaml\") as f:\n    config = yaml.safe_load(f)\n\n# Create agents from config\nagents = {}\nfor name, cfg in config[\"agents\"].items():\n    agents[name] = Agent(\n        role=cfg[\"role\"],\n        goal=cfg[\"goal\"],\n        backstory=cfg[\"backstory\"],\n        llm=cfg[\"llm\"],\n        verbose=cfg.get(\"verbose\", False),\n    )\n\n# Create tasks from config\ntasks = []\nfor name, cfg in config[\"tasks\"].items():\n    tasks.append(Task(\n        description=cfg[\"description\"],\n        agent=agents[cfg[\"agent\"]],\n        expected_output=cfg[\"expected_output\"],\n    ))\n\n# Run crew\ncrew = Crew(\n    agents=list(agents.values()),\n    tasks=tasks,\n    process=Process.sequential if config[\"crew\"][\"process\"] == \"sequential\" else Process.hierarchical,\n    verbose=config[\"crew\"].get(\"verbose\", True),\n)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import sys\n    topic = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"AI agent deployment best practices\"\n    result = crew.kickoff(inputs={\"topic\": topic})\n    print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\\nFINAL OUTPUT:\\n{'='*60}\\n{result}\")\n"
  },
